## BYL — current state
29. 6'4", lean-hard, black hair, deep blue eyes, unkempt. Orange safety vest with arc-flash burn over left ribs; brown boots, steel through right toe cap. 40-lb canvas tool bag. Blunt, sarcastic, tired. Yakuza killed his mother and younger sisters ten years ago. Played cello at a nationally recognized level as a boy; quit when they died. Trash apartment full of salvaged parts (Fasco blower in the walkway, coffee cans of capacitors, hand-rewound stator). Two university classes: **metallurgy** (useful for work) and a **linguistics** course he took because the room was air-conditioned — turned out he loves it. ~40 credits toward nothing. Studied under **old Nakagawa**, retiring repairman, who now refers him work.
- **The dream:** white courtyard, no shadows, he's ~11 and drops an armored man in four seconds; girls screaming his name from the colonnade; then the silver-haired woman at the top of the stair, looking at him "like a tool she's about to spend." Same dream nightly for ten years. Can never hold the name.
- **Lucy:** golden retriever, no leash, no collar. Waits *outside* fence lines. Trained bite-hold. Reads his moods. Wanders off to find people to play with. Dead gray tennis ball, no felt left.
- Scars: unstitched ridge from trapezius across collarbone, one across ribs, long seam wrist-to-elbow, round burn marks at the crook.
 
## WHO HAS MET HIM — chapter by chapter
 
**1. Byl's apartment / rooftop of Kaiyo Tower** — wakes from dream, talks to Lucy, gets Tomo's text, goes to fix the highrise chiller (jumpered a welded contactor; real part next day).
 
**2. Michiru (Kaiyo Tower roof).** Ruined oil painting, damp violin, called management twice. Went to the roof barefoot in a sea-green slip, no makeup, no jewelry. Played **Vasarhelyi's *Kis szomorú tánc* ("Little Sad Dance," 1909)** — hitched the fourth section trying to lift it. Three men applauded from behind the chiller. Two ogled her; Byl read her violin. She baited him with the over-tightening line; he corrected her instantly and exposed himself. Her line: *"only a man who can truly appreciate a rare instrument appreciates it with his eyes before he appreciates a rare beauty."* He named the piece and gave her the fix — **take the turn down an octave onto the G, drag it, let the tempo go slack** — then fled while she was hearing it. She played it his way; best thing she's made in three years. Thought she'd never see him again. **Sprite Lens: done.**
 
**3. Rei (Hikawa Shrine).** Father dead a year; eleven months of estate work; shrine decaying. Yakuza pair visited that morning (ink at the wrists), complimented her face, said she needed looking after; she shut them down cold. She whirled on Byl thinking he was them. He gave her the save with the Alphard line. Relayed **Nakagawa's warning verbatim**: *"She's a beautiful girl in a lonely shrine so don't you dare make a move on her. She's a gem in this world. Do a good job and you might be lucky like me to keep getting a glimpse at it."* — "That's for the greeting. Figured we'd start square." Replaced 7+ tiles and underlayment on the NE run, straightened 40 ft of fence. **Rei's recognition:** Lucy sat outside the fence line → memory of a well-dressed boy of 18–19 who came twice a week at 14, argued with the air — *"Why do men like that get to exist. Answer me that first. Then bring them back."* She never told him. Paid extra; he returned the overage — *rate before the job, not a favor after.* Flagged the third stair step as next. She trusts him. **Sprite Lens: done.**
 
**4. Ami (Byl's own building's roof).** Moved out of her mother's on purpose to feel financial strain; 20 classes, tests out, med school at year's end; rewired her own apartment. Tore into the 22-year-old rooftop unit to kill an aperiodic tick (fragment of blower guard, beat frequency). Byl sent up by the landlord. They rebuilt it together; **she reflashed the control board** and killed the phantom defrost routine — his "*What* are you." She praised the unknown maintainer's ingenuity at length ("a person doing Fourier analysis with their hands," "I'd like to take his brain apart") until he went scarlet. Two hours in a soaked white shirt, no bra, cutoff shorts — **he never once looked**, held her eyes when he thanked her. She noticed after; called him a gentleman; then wished he hadn't been (his hands around her waist), shut it down with Dutton & Aron 1974. **Never got his name.** **Sprite Lens: done.**
 
**5. Makoto (Kenji's diner, midnight).** Dating **Kenji**, 32, six foot, owns the diner, reminds her of Sempai; boring-adjacent, stressed, going soft. She's loaned him ~¥410,000 since October and tonight added **¥200,000** more — five months of green flowers off the flower-shop calendar. Condition: she gets to see the real books. Byl came for the grill (carbon on the left manifold gas valve seat; rich pilot sooting the orifice — 20-minute fix, dirt cheap). Kenji was rude and jealous, probed her "type," muttered about her three jobs; she drew the line: *"I look. And at two in the morning I come home to you."* Byl exited with **"Thanks for the entertainment."** Both flushed scarlet. Kenji apologized (it's the money), she hugged him — and noted he never said thank you for the ¥200,000. Lucy waited outside in the alley. **Sprite Lens: done.**
 
**6. Minako (dead machine-parts district, ~8:40 pm).** Post-shoot, full glam, mesh cocktail dress. Boyfriend **Ryō**, 26, junior manager at the talent division — pretty, connected, loyal, catastrophically boring; five months, her longest of four relationships in three years. Saw five men follow Byl into an alley. Byl had bloodied three of them the week before for wrecking an old man's rice shop on collection day. Fight in progress: one down bleeding, Lucy holding one, Byl against three with a skip covering his flank. **She jumped in without transforming** — kicked her heels off, put one into pallets, wrist-locked another; the last ran shouting *bakemono ka*. Scalp split (4 butterflies), eyebrow (2), deltoid contusion, split knuckles. He refused treatment and showed her his scars; **Lucy whined and he caved.** She dressed him at a gas station under the canopy while strangers stared. He clocked her technique ("a medic's habit," "somebody taught you that"); she hedged (kickboxing in Meguro, "I watched a video") and he let it lie both times. She noticed he's the complete opposite of the pretty boys she picks. **She took his number** — "that's the price of the butterflies." **Sprite Lens: done.**
 
**7. Hotaru (college quad, ginkgo bench, 11:40).** Unofficial fan club — **Kaburagi** with his folder, five awkward second-years, film society Tarkovsky screening **Friday 7pm, annex room 202**; she said she *might* come after her 7:30 seminar (huge for her). Michiru's line she keeps on an index card in a drawer: *"you don't have to be good at it, you only have to keep showing up to it."* Lucy brought her the dead ball; ten throws, she ran on the quad and laughed out loud. Byl arrived; she blushed and apologized. They sat in the grass an hour trading throws. Both relaxed visibly. His line to her: *"everybody I know who knew at nineteen isn't doing it anymore."* She made the half-hearted study offer; **numbers traded**; he offered Lucy visits any time.
 
**8. Michiru & Hotaru, dinner at home (kaiseki delivery, Michiru POV).** Michiru's news: **Kurosawa Jun**, "rival" violinist, 6'1"–6'2", black hair, charcoal three-piece to a *rehearsal*, sharing the Bartók program in November. His line about the "specific loneliness of playing this well." She's going to say yes — openly admits it's vanity: she wants someone who fits the foyer, who won't need managing, who understands the fourth section without explanation. First man she's considered since Haruka. Hotaru told her about the dog and the giant → Michiru revealed the roof encounter. **"Twice is a coincidence. Three times is a fact."** She intends to collect the third. Told Hotaru to bring him round — piano nobody plays, she'll feed him properly; *"He wouldn't come if I asked."* End beat: she wiped two weeks of dust off the closed piano lid, didn't lift it, then played the Vasarhelyi his way by the black glass.
